"# Lead-flow verification for web agencies

_Stage: new · Model: claude-x · Prompt: case-write.v1_

## Summary

**One-liner:** Daily synthetic test leads through every client site's quote form, confirmed all the way to the inbox or CRM, sold to the agency that maintains the sites.

**Buyer:** Small web and marketing agencies that maintain 20-100 small-business client sites on retainer. They, not the plumber, see the same broken-form failure across many sites, take the blame when leads stop, and need proof that their maintenance retainer is worth paying for.

**Problem:** A contact or quote form shows its success message, but a plugin update, SMTP change or CRM integration failure means the lead never arrives. Uptime monitors and analytics still report healthy, so the failure is silent until the client notices a dry pipeline weeks later.

**Solution:** One engine submits a tagged test lead through each client site's real form on a schedule and checks that it lands at the destination (inbox, CRM or webhook). When it does not arrive, the agency gets an alert naming the site and the broken step, and every month gets a per-client report proving the lead path worked.

**Price:** $8 per site per month. Priced per monitored site so it scales with the agency's book and can be passed through on the client's maintenance invoice; well under the value of a single recovered lead.

**Why now:** WordPress plugin churn and the move to authenticated email sending mean form delivery breaks more often, while agencies are under pressure to justify retainers with visible proof of work.

**Why it wins:** Uptime and browser-automation tools stop at 'the page loaded' or 'the form submitted'. This is the only level that confirms the lead reached the business, and it is sold to the aggregator who feels the pain on every client site.

**Next action:** Interview five agency owners who maintain 30+ client sites, then run a free 30-day pilot on one agency's sites and show them the first silent failure it catches.

## For you to check

This case has no checked sources — verify everything yourself.

- **Signal:** Our forms die after plugin updates ([news.example](https://news.example/item/1)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Number input:** price.unitsPerBuyer: 40 ([agency-benchmarks.example](https://agency-benchmarks.example/2026-small-agency-report)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Number input:** problemCost\\[0\\].unitCost (lost leads from broken forms): 400 ([trades-marketing.example](https://trades-marketing.example/average-lead-value-home-services)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Number input:** reachableBuyers: 3000 ([agency-directory.example](https://agency-directory.example/web-design-agencies-canada-us)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Competitor:** Generic uptime monitor ([uptime-tool.example](https://uptime-tool.example/pricing)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Competitor pricing:** Generic uptime monitor pricing: $15/month for 50 monitors ([uptime-tool.example](https://uptime-tool.example/pricing)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Competitor:** Synthetic browser testing platform ([synthetic-tests.example](https://synthetic-tests.example/pricing)): not checked yet — open it yourself
- **Competitor pricing:** Synthetic browser testing platform pricing: From $99/month ([synthetic-tests.example](https://synthetic-tests.example/pricing)): not checked yet — open it yourself

## Evidence

### Signals

- "Our forms die after plugin updates" (Hacker News, [news.example](https://news.example/item/1)) not checked

### Claims

_No claims recorded._

## Numbers

### Key results

- Annual price per buyer: $3,840
- Annual problem cost per buyer: $96,000
- Annual savings per buyer: $48,000
- ROI multiple: 12.5x
- Payback: 0.96 months
- Annual revenue potential: $11,520,000
- Year 1 revenue: $115,200
- Gross margin: 87.5%
- Breakeven buyers: 1

### Formulas

- Annual price = $8 × 40 × 12 = $3,840
- Annual cost of lost leads from broken forms = 6 × $400 × 40 = $96,000
- Annual problem cost = $96,000
- Annual savings = $96,000 × 0.5 = $48,000
- ROI multiple = annual savings $48,000 ÷ annual price $3,840 = 12.5×
- Payback = annual price $3,840 ÷ (annual savings $48,000 ÷ 12) = 0.96 months
- Monthly price per buyer = $3,840 / 12 = $320
- Monthly delivery cost per buyer = $40
- Gross margin = (monthly price $320 − delivery $40) ÷ $320 = 87.5%
- Annual revenue potential = 3000 × $3,840 = $11,520,000
- Year 1 revenue = $11,520,000 × 0.01 = $115,200
- Breakeven buyers = ceil($30 / ($320 - $40)) = 1

### Inputs

| Input | Value | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| price.amount | 8 | assumption: Our proposed price per monitored site per month, set well below the value of one lead. |
| price.unitsPerBuyer | 40 | [agency-benchmarks.example](https://agency-benchmarks.example/2026-small-agency-report): "The median agency in our survey maintains 40 client websites on a monthly care plan." |
| problemCost\\[0\\].quantity (lost leads from broken forms) | 6 | assumption: Leads lost per silent form failure before anyone notices (roughly three weeks of enquiries for a small trades business). |
| problemCost\\[0\\].unitCost (lost leads from broken forms) | 400 | [trades-marketing.example](https://trades-marketing.example/average-lead-value-home-services): "For home-service businesses, the average value of a qualified inbound lead is about $400." |
| problemCost\\[0\\].perYear (lost leads from broken forms) | 40 | assumption: One silent failure per client site per year across the agency's 40 sites. |
| expectedReduction | 0.5 | assumption: Daily checks catch failures within a day, recovering about half of the leads that would otherwise be lost. |
| reachableBuyers | 3000 | [agency-directory.example](https://agency-directory.example/web-design-agencies-canada-us): "Our directory lists 3,000 web design agencies in Canada and the US that advertise website maintenance plans." |
| captureRate | 0.01 | assumption: 1% of reachable agencies buy in year one from cold outreach. |
| deliveryCostPerBuyerMonthly\\[0\\] (infra+LLM) | 40 | assumption: Headless browser runs, test inboxes and LLM triage for 40 sites per month. |
| fixedCostsMonthly\\[0\\] (hosting) | 30 | assumption: One small VPS plus database for the scheduler. |

### Scenarios

| Buyers | MRR | ARR | Monthly gross profit | Monthly net |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 10 | $3,200 | $38,400 | $2,800 | $2,770 |
| 50 | $16,000 | $192,000 | $14,000 | $13,970 |
| 200 | $64,000 | $768,000 | $56,000 | $55,970 |

